### Describe the bug

Setting `fakeTimers.toNotFake` silently causes `queueMicrotask` to be faked, contradicting the documented default.

[The docs](https://vitest.dev/config/faketimers) say `toFake` defaults to "everything available globally except `nextTick` and `queueMicrotask`", and `toNotFake` defaults to `[]`. So `toNotFake: ['Temporal']` should subtract one API from that set. Instead it *adds* `queueMicrotask` faking, which hangs promise-driven code.

The cause is in `FakeTimers.useFakeTimers()`: Vitest's own default is only computed when **both** options are unset, so naming `toNotFake` skips it and falls through to `@sinonjs/fake-timers`' default, which fakes everything.

```js
let toFake = this._userConfig?.toFake;
let toNotFake = this._userConfig?.toNotFake;
if (toFake === void 0 && toNotFake === void 0)
  // only reached when BOTH are unset
  toFake = Object.keys(this._fakeTimers.timers).filter(
    timer => timer !== 'nextTick' && timer !== 'queueMicrotask'
  );
```

This is easy to hit because the [v5 migration guide recommends exactly this pattern](https://vitest.dev/guide/migration/) for keeping `Temporal` native:

> `Temporal` is part of the default set of faked APIs... To keep `Temporal` native, add it to `toNotFake`:
> ```ts
> vi.useFakeTimers({ toNotFake: ['Temporal'] })
> ```

Following that advice turns on `queueMicrotask` faking as a side effect.

`nextTick` escapes only incidentally, via the separate `isChildProcess()` guard that re-adds it.

