### Describe the bug

`ensureCacheIntegrity()` compares the lockfile hash against `_metadata.json` and wipes the cache when it differs. But `clearCache()` removes the whole directory, `_metadata.json` included, and the file is never rewritten. On the next lockfile change there is no metadata, so it takes the "just store a new one, don't reset the cache" branch and stale entries survive.

When the deps optimizer is active, transformed modules embed `?v=<browserHash>` on every node_modules import, and that hash is derived from the lockfile. Stale entries import `left-pad?v=<old>` while `vi.mock('left-pad')` registers against `?v=<new>`: different module id, mock never applies, no error.

Affects 4.1.x and 5.0.0.

